! jb_af1c "PAU GATES ROUTINE", the SRTE30 check, p.195 and p.199
! (octal 023666.40-023673.00): STORE ROOT of a radicand with a single
! fraction bit AND AN ODD EXPONENT.
!
! WHY THIS ONE.  Every square-root case transcribed so far -- CHKSSR's
! fourteen single-bit positions and the four multi-bit perfect squares
! -- has an EVEN exponent, because the radicand is built by a VFL load
! that leaves the exponent field zero.  This block is the first that
! does not: after loading the fraction bit it ADDS a one into IBM 10,
! which is the low bit of EM, making the exponent +1.
!
! WHAT THAT TRIPS.  p.95: a square root halves the exponent, so an odd
! exponent must be made even first, and the model does it by shifting
! the fraction right one and adding one to the exponent.  Here the
! fraction is a SINGLE bit at IBM 59 -- the very bottom of the
! fraction -- so a right shift of one would push it out entirely and
! the root would come back zero.
!
! AND THE BLOCK CALLS THAT AN ERROR.  Its branch is BBZ, not the BZB
! every other check uses: BZB branches when the indicator is ZERO ("the
! compare failed"), BBZ branches when it is ONE.  So this halts when
! RZ is on -- when the root came out zero -- and its message says why:
! "SHIFT R1-BIT LOST".  The block exists to assert that the bit is NOT
! lost.
!
! That makes it a direct test of something no transcribed block has
! reached, and a prediction worth recording before running it: if the
! model drops the bit, this halts at SRTE30.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes: SERS (octal 1304) -> FAIL halt,
! -- SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch.
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- data (pp.199-200) --
        SLC, (8)24122.0
WRDB    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1252525252525250000000
        DD(BU,64,8), (8)0525252525252524000000
        SLC, (8)24237.0
SRSG    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000000000000000000000

        SLC, (8)23666.40
SR30    L(BU,1), WRDB, 68                    ! a single fraction bit at IBM 59
        +(BU,1), WRDB, 117                   ! and a one into IBM 10: exponent +1
        SRT(U), SRSG
        BBZ, $RZ, SRTE30                     ! halt if the root came out ZERO
        B, $+1.32
SRTE30  SIC, SEN
        B, SERS                              ! shift r1-bit lost
PASS    BEW, $
        END, SR30
